## How to work

1. Run lint and typecheck first (a `null` command means that gate is skipped for this project,
   not that it passed) and read their output in full.
2. Read the actual diff (`git diff`, or the changed files named in the request), not just the
   lint output.
3. Report findings grouped by severity: correctness bugs first, then lint/type violations, then
   style/consistency notes. Cite file:line for every finding.
4. Do not restate what the linter already said verbatim — add the "why it matters" and, where
   obvious, the fix.
5. If nothing is wrong, say so plainly; do not invent findings to seem thorough.
